invariant: INV-44
file: p384.c
catches: test/widemul-builds.sh
reason: p384.c chooses its arm on a define no build passes, so a host
  object compiles the 32-bit arithmetic and never calls
  p384_wide_verify.c. test/widemul-builds.sh compiles the file as a
  host object does and requires its call into p384_wide_verify.c and
  none into p384_field.c. The file picks its arm in one place, so this
  edit compiles under every compiler.

--- old
#ifdef CH_CPU_RUNTIME

#include "p384_wide_verify.h"
--- new
#ifdef CH_CPU_HOST

#include "p384_wide_verify.h"
